---
title: Choices
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

`ShowChoice` asks the player to pick from a list of options, and puts the number of the one they picked in `LVar0`. Options count from `0`.

Show the question first, with a message that ends with `[Yield][End]` so its box stays open, then answer with `ContinueSpeech`:

```c
Call(SpeakToPlayer, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Talk, ANIM_Goombaria_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_0098)
Call(ShowChoice, MSG_Choice_0011)
IfEq(LVar0, 0)
    Call(ContinueSpeech, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Talk, ANIM_Goombaria_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_009A)
Else
    Call(ContinueSpeech, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Talk, ANIM_Goombaria_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_0099)
EndIf
```

The options are a message too. `msg/1E_Choices.msg` has the game's, such as `Choice_0011`, which is Yes or No:

```
#message:1E:(Choice_0011) {
	[Style choice pos=120,90 size=75,46]
	[DelayOff]
	[Cursor 0][Option 0]Yes[BR]
	[Cursor 1][Option 1]No[BR]
	[Option 255][DelayOn]
	[SetCancel 1][EndChoice 2][End]
}
```

To write your own, copy one with the same number of options and change its text:

- `[Cursor n][Option n]` comes before option `n`.
- `[SetCancel 1]` picks option `1` when the player presses B.
- `[EndChoice 2]` is the number of options.
- `pos` and `size` in `[Style choice]` set where the box is and how big it is.
